# PROJECT_NAME — agent context

> Generated by `orch init --template python-api` (GENERATED_AT).

## Stack

- Python `>=3.11`
- FastAPI `>=0.115,<0.116` (Starlette 1.0 breaks the legacy `TemplateResponse` — pin the ceiling)
- `uvicorn[standard]` for the dev server
- Dev: `pytest`, `ruff`, `httpx` (FastAPI TestClient uses it)

## Layout

- `app/` — application package (`app.main:app` is the ASGI entry)
- `tests/` — pytest, discovered via default rootdir
- `.orchestrator/` — orch state (config, model router, SQLite)

## Conventions

- Every route change ships with a test in the same PR — no exceptions.
- Run `pytest -q` before pushing; the shipped CI workflow runs the same command.
- Type-check by running the tests, not a separate `mypy` invocation.

## Orch state

- SQLite at `.orchestrator/state/PROJECT_NAME/orch.db`.
- `tasks_definition` (static): id, model, backend, deps, phase, estimate.
- `tasks_runtime` (dynamic): status, attempts, last_model, last_backend.
- **Never edit runtime status in `tasks.json`** — use `orch task set --id ID --status STATUS` instead.

## Useful commands

```bash
orch status                              # human table
orch tasks --status todo,in-progress     # narrower view
orch run --dry-run                       # preview the plan
orch dashboard --profile stakeholder     # share the URL with your client
```
